{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>Say to the priests.</b> 'Say' and 'you shall say' — to warn the great about the small (Yevamot 114)." "<b>The sons of Aaron.</b> One might think disqualified priests [lit. profaned ones] — therefore Scripture says 'the priests'." "<b>The sons of Aaron.</b> Also priests with blemishes are included in the meaning." "<b>The sons of Aaron.</b> And not the daughters of Aaron (Sifra)." "<b>He shall not defile himself among his people.</b> While the dead is among his people — this excludes a mitzvah-death [i.e., an unattended corpse for which there is a mitzvah to bury it] (there)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:07:30.196708041Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}